{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 38, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**Summary of the Wikipedia page \"Raymond III Count of Tripoli\"**\n\nRaymond III (c. 1140–1187) was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III became count at the age of twelve after his father was assassinated in 1152. During his minority his mother Hodierna ruled as regent. In 1164 he was captured at the Battle of Harim and held prisoner in Aleppo until 1172. Upon his release he returned to Tripoli where he resumed his role as count and also acted as regent for his young cousin King Baldwin IV of Jerusalem from 1174 to 1177.\n\n*highlighted section part 1*\n\nAs regent Raymond III played a crucial role in the politics of the Crusader states. He supported the faction of the Count of Flanders against the faction of the Count of Anjou in the succession dispute over the Kingdom of Jerusalem. In 1176 he arranged the marriage of Baldwin IV to Princess Theodora Komnene which strengthened his position. Raymond also negotiated truces with Saladin and other Muslim leaders to secure the borders of Tripoli and Jerusalem.\n\nIn 1177 Raymond III led a crusader army to victory against Saladin at the Battle of Montgisard. This victory temporarily halted Saladins advance into the Crusader states. However by 1187 Raymonds health was failing and he was unable to prevent Saladins conquest of most of the Kingdom of Jerusalem after the disastrous Battle of Hattin.\n\n*highlighted section part 2*\n\nRaymond III died childless in 1187 and the County of Tripoli passed to his kinsman Raymond of Antioch. His death marked the end of an era for the Crusader states. Raymond III is remembered as a capable ruler and a skilled diplomat who worked to maintain the fragile balance of power between the Crusader states and their Muslim neighbors.\n\n*highlighted section part 3*\n\nRaymond IIIs reign saw significant developments in the politics and warfare of the Crusader states. His regency for Baldwin IV was particularly important as he navigated the complex political landscape of the time. Despite his eventual failures Raymond III remains a notable figure in the history of the Crusades.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.2467155009508133}, {"token": "Summary", "logprob": -0.9313726425170898}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0005951540661044419}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.11428595334291458}, {"token": " Wikipedia", "logprob": -7.283422019099817e-05}, {"token": " page", "logprob": -0.34850868582725525}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.17936432361602783}, {"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.00012575789878610522}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.6954811548639555e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -5.3165931603871286e-05}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.005993844475597143}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.649054244509898e-05}, {"token": " Tripoli", "logprob": -1.7881377516459906e-06}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.0010832638945430517}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logprob": -5.674201020156033e-05}, {"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.12037494033575058}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -1.5497195136049413e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -3.683499380713329e-05}, {"token": " (", "logprob": -2.423067092895508}, {"token": "c", "logprob": -0.13397683203220367}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.005947155877947807}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.007748901844024658}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -4.0531076592742465e-06}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0003631647559814155}, {"token": "4", "logprob": -0.0012500813463702798}, {"token": "0", "logprob": -0.06240718811750412}, {"token": "–", "logprob": -0.4687783718109131}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0009018882992677391}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0003502947511151433}, {"token": "8", "logprob": -0.0007965967524796724}, {"token": "7", "logprob": -0.00031382881570607424}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.00013302871957421303}, {"token": " was"